{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "name": "Titanium.UI.iOS.NavigationWindow",
  "kind": "view",
  "extends": "Titanium.UI.Window",
  "inheritanceChain": [
    "Titanium.UI.Window",
    "Titanium.UI.View",
    "Titanium.Proxy"
  ],
  "platforms": [
    "iphone",
    "ipad",
    "macos"
  ],
  "since": {
    "iphone": "3.1.3",
    "ipad": "3.1.3",
    "macos": "9.2.0"
  },
  "deprecated": {
    "since": "8.0.0",
    "removed": "10.0.0",
    "notes": "Use [Titanium.UI.NavigationWindow](Titanium.UI.NavigationWindow) instead."
  },
  "summary": "A `NavigationWindow` implements a specialized view that manages the navigation of hierarchical\ncontent.\n",
  "description": "You create a `NavigationWindow` with the [Titanium.UI.iOS.createNavigationWindow](api:Titanium.UI.iOS#createNavigationWindow) factory method, or\na `<NavigationWindow>` Alloy element.\n\nAll `NavigationWindow` objects must have at least one root window that cannot be removed. When\ncreating a `NavigationWindow` with the factory method, you must set its `window` property to the\nroot level window. Equivalently, in an Alloy application, insert a `<Window>` element as a child of the\n`<NavigationWindow>` element. See examples below.\n\nThis object is not meant to be added to other windows. However, it can be used within a [Titanium.UI.iOS.SplitWindow](api:Titanium.UI.iOS.SplitWindow).\n",
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Simple Navigation Window",
      "code": "Creates a navigation window with the first window colored red.\nPress the button to open the blue window.\nUse the back button to return to the red root window.\n\n``` js\nvar win2 = Ti.UI.createWindow({\n    backgroundColor: 'red',\n    title: 'Red Window'\n});\n\nvar win1 = Ti.UI.iOS.createNavigationWindow({\n    window: win2\n});\n\nvar win3 = Ti.UI.createWindow({\n    backgroundColor: 'blue',\n    title: 'Blue Window'\n});\n\nvar button = Ti.UI.createButton({\n    title: 'Open Blue Window'\n});\nbutton.addEventListener('click', function(){\n    win1.openWindow(win3, {animated:true});\n});\n\nwin2.add(button);\nvar button2 = Titanium.UI.createButton({\n    title: 'Close Blue Window'\n});\nbutton2.addEventListener('click', function(){\n    win1.closeWindow(win3, {animated:false}); //win3.close() will also work!!\n});\n\nwin3.add(button2);\nwin1.open();\n```\n"
    },
    {
      "title": "Alloy XML Markup",
      "code": "Previous example as two Alloy view-controllers.  Requires Alloy 1.2.2 and later.\n\napp/views/index.xml:\n``` xml\n<Alloy>\n    <NavigationWindow id=\"win1\" platform=\"ios\">\n        <Window id=\"win2\" title=\"Red Window\" backgroundColor=\"red\">\n            <Button id=\"button\" onClick=\"openBlueWindow\">Open Blue Window</Button>\n        </Window>\n    </NavigationWindow>\n</Alloy>\n```\n\napp/controllers/index.js:\n``` js\nfunction openBlueWindow(e) {\n    var win3 = Alloy.createController('bluewin').getView();\n    $.win1.openWindow(win3);\n}\n\n$.win1.open();\n```\n\napp/views/bluewin.xml:\n``` xml\n<Alloy>\n    <Window id=\"win3\" title=\"Blue Window\" backgroundColor=\"blue\">\n        <Button onClick=\"closeWindow\">Close Window</Button>\n    </Window>\n</Alloy>\n```\n\napp/controllers/bluewin.js:\n``` js\nfunction closeWindow(){\n    $.win3.close();\n}\n```\n"
    }
  ],
  "properties": [
    {
      "name": "window",
      "platforms": [
        "iphone",
        "ipad",
        "macos"
      ],
      "summary": "Window to add to this navigation window.",
      "type": [
        {
          "kind": "type",
          "name": "Titanium.UI.Window"
        }
      ],
      "availability": "creation"
    }
  ],
  "methods": [
    {
      "name": "closeWindow",
      "platforms": [
        "iphone",
        "ipad",
        "macos"
      ],
      "summary": "Closes a window and removes it from the navigation window.",
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "window",
          "summary": "Window to close.",
          "type": [
            {
              "kind": "type",
              "name": "Titanium.UI.Window"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "options",
          "summary": "Options supporting a single `animated` boolean property to determine whether the window\nwill be animated (default) while being closed (default: true).\n",
          "type": [
            {
              "kind": "type",
              "name": "Dictionary"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "openWindow",
      "platforms": [
        "iphone",
        "ipad",
        "macos"
      ],
      "summary": "Opens a window within the navigation window.",
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "window",
          "summary": "Window to open.",
          "type": [
            {
              "kind": "type",
              "name": "Titanium.UI.Window"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "options",
          "summary": "Options supporting a single `animated` boolean property to determine whether the window\nwill be animated (default) while being opened (default: true).\n",
          "type": [
            {
              "kind": "type",
              "name": "Dictionary"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "popToRootWindow",
      "platforms": [
        "iphone",
        "ipad",
        "macos"
      ],
      "summary": "Closes all windows that are currently opened inside the navigation window.",
      "description": "Note that only the `close` event of the most recently opened window is fired.",
      "since": "6.0.0",
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "options",
          "summary": "Options supporting a single `animated` boolean property to determine whether the windows\nwill be animated while being closed (default: false).\n",
          "type": [
            {
              "kind": "type",
              "name": "Dictionary"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
